Stage 07 Task 03 — World Persistence and Upgrade.

This PR closes `plans/07-hardening/✅-03-world-upgrade.md` without starting Task 04.

Implemented:
- explicit v2 SavedData schemas for tectonic stress, volcano sites/chambers and geological deposits;
- released unversioned payloads treated as v1 and migrated on next write;
- corrupt known-schema entries isolated with actionable logging;
- unknown future schemas fail closed/read-only so runtime cannot overwrite unfamiliar state;
- existing generated chunks remain excluded from automatic volcano site registration/terrain shaping;
- `/volcanoes world_upgrade preview <chunk_x> <chunk_z>` plus one-shot `/volcanoes world_upgrade apply <token>` for explicit metadata-only existing-world registration;
- preview/apply validates dimension, seed, expiry, candidate identity and persisted spacing and never invokes terrain shaping.

TDD evidence:
- RED: Performance Hardening Acceptance `33348850851` failed before `ExistingWorldVolcanoAdminSession` existed.
- GREEN code-head `40e7d562ca7c9f99c9f9de2566e205a5a522581a`: Volcanoes CI `33349268687`, Performance `33349268707`, Create/Sable `33349268718`, Cold Sweat `33349268708`, RNS `33349268676`, MineColonies `33349268681`.

Final exact-head verification is running on `e01a2b9c26e7944d2248f20986e0f348bf783588`. Merge is blocked until all eight canonical gates are GREEN and PR review/thread state is clean.

## Scope

Closes the remaining Stage 06 RNS integration blocker with exact-host coexistence rather than unsafe global metal-family ownership transfer.

Canonical contract:
- Volcanoes physically owns only its bounded hydrothermal Cu/Fe/Au ore bodies;
- native RNS worldgen remains enabled for every protected metal family: Cu/Fe/Au/Sn/Ni/Zn/Ag;
- the lifecycle bridge projects only already-authoritative Volcanoes Cu/Fe/Au deposits as RNS custom/scannable locations;
- tin, nickel, zinc and silver remain entirely RNS-owned and are rejected by the Volcanoes projection planner;
- no global RNS metal family is disabled;
- exact host mismatch, missing KubeJS surface, missing projected selection, or loss of protected native worldgen fails closed.

## TDD / review evidence

Two review findings were reproduced as failing contracts before the production fixes:
- planner-level rejection of non-produced Sn/Ni/Zn/Ag projections;
- native-worldgen preservation for all seven protected RNS metal families.

RED evidence: Volcanoes CI `33308431809` failed at Unit tests on `c2d0b20cd3d2fa19abd172ae62ea41bef839b748` before production was changed.

Both review threads were then fixed, replied to, and resolved.

## Exact current head

`4e2b772fb1bbe30cfaa1c55d99de1ead4660b35b`

