A fresh `@codex review` was requested for this exact head after the fixes.

## Scope

Public documentation/governance pass only; no gameplay implementation is changed.

- expands the root README from the canonical `plans/` state, separating implemented systems from remaining roadmap;
- documents Geology, Tectonics, volcano lifecycle, atmosphere/respiration, pressure and optional integration authority boundaries;
- adds the project BSD-2-Clause `LICENSE` already declared by Gradle metadata;
- adds root `SOURCES.md` and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`;
- preserves and clarifies the existing TFC Volcanoes upstream notice/inventory;
- adds a Stage 07 third-party license/provenance hardening task and strengthens the release checklist;
- packages `LICENSE` and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` in the built JAR;
- removes stale “private modpack” wording from project metadata.

The provenance gate is fail-closed: external dependencies/references do not become source-reuse grants, and any actual copied/adapted source or asset must have exact upstream revision/file provenance plus applicable notice/permission before release.

This PR intentionally does not modify the active Stage 07 persistence PRs or the remaining RNS gameplay work.

## Scope

Implements the bounded physical hydrothermal ore producer required before any RNS ownership handoff.

- deterministically plans bounded hydrothermal ore placement;
- materializes exact Stage 01 copper, iron and gold families into natural stone/deepslate hosts;
- fails closed when full target coverage cannot be satisfied;
- prevalidates host state before writes and rolls back failed application;
- propagates an explicit physical-realization proof through geothermal handoff/runtime state;
- adds NeoForge GameTests that physically verify copper, iron and gold blocks on the dedicated GameTest server.

## RNS safety

This PR deliberately does **not** disable native RNS worldgen and does **not** re-enable the RNS lifecycle bridge. Exact metadata remains insufficient by itself; ownership transfer is a separate step after this physical producer is proven by CI and the global ownership semantics are audited.

Tin, nickel, zinc and silver remain outside Volcanoes ownership scope.

## Scope

This PR resolves the canonical hydrothermal mineral-identity blocker in core geology without prematurely transferring physical ore worldgen ownership from Create Rock & Stone.

### Core geology
- adds `HydrothermalMineralizationPolicy` for the Stage 01 metal families already recognized by Volcanoes;
- classifies shield/fissure hydrothermal systems as `c:ores/iron`, stratovolcano systems as `c:ores/copper`, and caldera systems as `c:ores/gold`;
- leaves purely tectonic hydrothermal systems generic as `volcanoes:resources/mineral`;
- exposes deterministic `GeothermalWorldgenResolver.causalVolcanoAt(...)`, selecting only a volcanic contribution that actually raises geothermal potential above the tectonic baseline;
- wires the production `HydrothermalDepositProjector` to that causal classification.

### World-upgrade compatibility
- preserves the existing hydrothermal deposit UUID across the metadata schema upgrade;
- `DepositRegistry` permits exactly one migration shape: legacy `HYDROTHERMAL` + `volcanoes:resources/mineral` → canonical `c:ores/copper|iron|gold`, with identical center/radius/richness;
- exact→different-exact, exact→generic, MAGMATIC, geometry changes and richness changes continue to fail closed;
- migration replaces the authoritative entry in place, keeps registry cardinality stable, marks SavedData dirty and dispatches the exact upsert to lifecycle observers;
- runtime regression coverage proves a legacy generic deposit is upgraded and acknowledged by `GeothermalWorldgenRuntime.persistPending(...)` in one turn instead of remaining in retry/quarantine.

### Safety / RNS ownership
- does **not** disable any native RNS deposit worldgen;
- does **not** re-enable the production RNS lifecycle bridge;
- does **not** claim tin, nickel, zinc or silver as Volcanoes-owned;
- records explicitly that exact metadata is not equivalent to physical ore generation.

`plans/06-integrations/05-rns.md` intentionally remains OPEN. The next blocker is physical, deterministic hydrothermal ore generation for the exact Stage 01 families before any RNS ownership handoff.

### TDD evidence
- RED `aefaa5347241f633ef96ec75abec2735810b9de2`: mineral identity policy test failed before implementation.
- GREEN `386fd825f62dd38635820a696f719ba1c6680b06`: policy unit tests passed.
- RED `74562e0c7bdd79fe14d378c3de508dd83ce440cb`: causal-volcano contract failed before implementation.
- GREEN implementation `6fa5c1d00549d812e934c2293405fcd17d59683d`.
- RED `cb7c63fd3eb7e5a1ef300035f46fab8ddb34d2f9`: production projector contract failed before wiring.
- GREEN `aec8e5c58e087092bc1654ba72ceccc0cf265604`: unit tests and diff sanity passed with production wiring.
- REVIEW RED `0077f4856f85719c297f0a6e49297542e7413445`: legacy same-UUID generic→exact upgrade regression failed in CI `33290668926` at Unit tests before build/smoke.
- migration aperture tests additionally prove changed geometry/richness, reverse migration and exact-metal rewrites remain rejected.
- final runtime regression at HEAD `c75a7285cd04b9425f5bced10d2073ccbb5c2105` proves the legacy handoff converges without duplicate deposits or retry/quarantine.

Final PR head also includes architectural decision 15 and the corrected RNS plan state.

## Stage 04 — Pollution / Acid Rain

Implements the remaining runtime path for volcanic pollution without making Destroy a hard dependency.

- keeps publication authority separate from provenance-safe readback;
- creates stable per-interval gas/ash pollution pulses;
- routes gas to acid-rain/greenhouse and ash smoke to Destroy smog;
- leaves particulates in Volcanoes Atmosphere because verified Destroy 0.4.1 has no particulate pollution type;
- binds the verified NeoForge 1.21.1 Destroy API reflectively behind the exact-version gate;
- makes host publication idempotent per pollution component after partial failures;
- preserves the existing Atmosphere gas/ash bridges as standalone fallback, avoiding double application;
- adds focused tests for pulse identity, channel mapping, dedupe and retry behavior.

This PR is intentionally opened before plan checkboxes are changed so CI can validate the implementation first.

