Focused Stage04 Task02 closure for `ATM-06-CREATE-RESPIRATION`, based on canonical `main` `ccaaaa791a1dba33974c4d102713a41ab3816825`.

## Exact host contract
Verified against Create `6.0.10`:
- `DivingHelmetItem.isWornBy(...)` identifies the host breathing equipment;
- `BacktankUtil.getAllWithAir(...)` resolves available pressurized-air sources;
- `BacktankUtil.consumeAir(...)` is the host resource debit;
- Create's native `LivingBreatheEvent` listener is default/NORMAL priority and debits one backtank air unit every 20 ticks when it handles non-breathing;
- Create does not provide particulate, acid-gas or toxic-gas filtration.

## Implemented
- optional exact-version Create 6.0.10 bootstrap, fail-closed when absent/mismatched/linkage fails;
- host-neutral `CreateRespirationDecision`;
- concrete Create adapter using the verified helmet/backtank APIs;
- only `ProtectionCapability.OXYGEN_SUPPLY` is contributed — no implicit particulate/acid/toxic filtering;
- shared `ProtectionUseRegistry` / `ProtectionUseSession` across Pressure and Respiration so one physical host resource debit is memoized exactly once per player/tick/resource key;
- session cleanup on logout, clone, dimension change and level unload;
- debit cadence matches Create's 20-tick cadence; off-cadence protection can remain breathable without spending host air;
- Atmosphere's `LivingBreatheEvent` listener runs at `EventPriority.LOWEST`, after Create's native NORMAL listener. This prevents Volcanoes-triggered hypoxia from causing both Create native code and the Atmosphere transaction to debit the same backtank, and prevents Create from subsequently overwriting Atmosphere contaminant denial.

## Semantics verified
- safe atmosphere never spends host air;
- low O2 + Diving Helmet + available backtank supplies oxygen;
- missing/depleted equipment supplies nothing;
- oxygen supply removes hypoxia only; CO2, acid gas, toxic gas and particulate hazards remain independent;
- underwater/lava remain owned by Create/vanilla because Atmosphere exits fluid breathing early;
- absent/wrong Create version fails closed without making Create mandatory.

## TDD / CI
