## P1 #3 — crash-safe worldgen metadata handoff — audited RED specification only

Preparatory branch: `feat/03-geothermal-crash-handoff-after-authority-red`.
Current RED ref HEAD: `5e9d33a9ee80540f4471db8d788c0df8914fede5`.
Its tree is identical to the previously audited `c40f0fe5e5ec6af7020696224271304d29342412`; the two later commits only refactor duplicate test coverage and do not change the effective RED contract. The branch descends from `26a5a0a4...` and contains only tests after that production ancestry.

The audited RED requires:
1. serializable `GeothermalChunkHandoff` preserving exact world seed + placement;
2. successful worldgen writes a durable chunk receipt after physical mutation and before transient commit;
3. owner-chunk journal deduplicates by deterministic source ID and fails closed on conflicting contents;
4. journal capacity is checked before mutation; hard maximum 8 receipts/chunk is enforced by the persisted codec itself;
5. `ChunkEvent.Load` only tracks receipt-bearing loaded chunks and never becomes SavedData authority;
6. recovery uses `getChunkNow` only, never force-loads, and untracks unload/resolved chunks;
7. >2,048 currently loaded receipt chunks are not dropped — recovery tracks loaded chunk identities rather than using a fixed 2,048 receipt queue;
8. transient and durable recovery share one hard 16-attempt tick envelope: transient-only 16; recovery-only 2 chunks × <=8 receipts; mixed 8 transient + 1 recovery chunk × <=8 receipts;
9. uncommitted reservations and quarantined poison do not steal processable-work budget;
10. durable recovery with complete metadata authority prunes matching committed/quarantined transient work but never an uncommitted reservation;
11. poison durable receipts are isolated within their chunk batch so later valid receipts still progress;
12. no `RECOVERY_CAPACITY` queue and no independent second 16-item recovery drain.

The old reference GREEN `a34dd2cfdd902552415674ef421dd3e2689b6218` remains rejected: it has an unbounded persisted attachment list, a fixed `RECOVERY_CAPACITY=2048` admission queue and independent `persistRecovered()` drain. Only its deterministic receipt codec concept and worldgen receipt ordering are reusable.

NeoForge attachment persistence via `serialize(Codec)` / `setData`, and loaded-only `ServerChunkCache#getChunkNow`, are compatible with the target 1.21.x API. The RED remains unobserved: workflow `33135021307`, verify `98732942703`, again completed with `steps=null` before runner allocation.

